  "name": "anthropic-native-tool-changes",
  "note": "Upstream 9e05370b2 (mid-conversation system messages), anthropic native path: compat supportsMidConvoSystemMessages + supportsMidConvoToolChanges with an initial tool, so the request declares read_file (cache breakpoint), the __pi_deferred_placeholder__ and the later list_dir (defer_loading), and carries the mid-conversation-tool-changes beta. The first update lands between a tool call and its result: transformMessages holds it past the result and convertMessages holds it until the next assistant message, where it is flushed as {role:system, content:[text, tool_addition]}. The closing update (text + tool_removal) is flushed at the end and takes the conversation cache breakpoint. Non-last string user content stays a string. npm 0.85.1 predated the transcript model; it shipped in pi-ai 0.86.1, and the backend flipped to dist at the 0.87.1 re-pin (README rule). Upstream aa47cedce (#12067): a non-strict tool keeps its root additionalProperties; backend src until a release ships it (1.5.2 predates it), so this requires PI_UPSTREAM_SHA >= aa47cedce.",
